WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.080
Stop!

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.770
First thing, totally unrealistic.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.761
He just fired a nuclear
weapon from his shoulder.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.040
I'm Mark "Billy" Billingham.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.180
I spent 27 years in the military,

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.150
nine in the parachute regiment,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.240
17 to...plus years with the SAS.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.770
Since leaving the armed forces,

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.900
I then became head of security

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.050
for a number of A-lists,

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.930
including Angelina Jolie and Brad Pitt.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.010
And I'm currently now
working in the TV industry

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.485
as an adviser on "SAS: Who Dares Wins."

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.400
The equipment and the Little Birds,

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.830
what the helicopters use,
is probably quite right.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.300
That's exactly how you ride
into battle, like these do.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.517
Flying down the streets
the way that we see there

00:00:48.517 --> 00:00:49.930
is probably a bit unrealistic,

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:51.570
bearing in mind it's
a hostile environment.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.260
Now, don't get me wrong,

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.000
these things can fly under washing lines,

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:55.833
they're unbelievable,

00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:58.230
but I just find that a
little bit unrealistic.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.190
I'm guessing because of the timelines

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.849
they had to move in daylight.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.520
OK, the second phase I'm looking at now,

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.210
they're coming in in the Black Hawks

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.670
and delivering the troops
by what we call fast rope,

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.560
which is the ropes from
the side of the aircraft.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.230
The unrealism again in my eyes

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.271
is they're dropping right onto the target,

00:01:16.271 --> 00:01:17.787
broad daylight,

00:01:17.787 --> 00:01:19.980
and you're basically a sitting duck.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.730
As for running out

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.610
in front of a 50-cal weapon,

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.226
I think that's a little bit OTT.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.370
The grenade launcher from
the small-arms weapon there

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.890
is totally overkill.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.760
What it would do is fragmentation,

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.370
a little bit of a noise;

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.503
it certainly wouldn't burst into flame.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.300
OK, so the first incident you see there

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.810
is what they call a coach option,

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.310
where they're about to storm
a coach for whatever reason,

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.340
believing there's terrorists on it.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.140
Now, the drills and
skills and the equipment,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.550
back in the day, is actually very correct,

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.210
pretty spot-on.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.007
What we call rehearsals

00:02:12.007 --> 00:02:13.430
and what they're rehearsing there is

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:16.300
close-quarter battle, clearing a building,

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.150
a stronghold where hostages may be held.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.320
The drills and the skills, again,

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.153
exactly as they would have.

00:02:22.153 --> 00:02:24.100
This is a very sort of light roll;

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.920
they'll do this five or six times.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.200
This is a walk-through/talk-through,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.360
then they'll do it a little bit faster,

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.100
and then eventually they
do it in full equipment.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.492
So, what I'm seeing there
is actually pretty accurate.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.820
The effects of a grenade is exactly that.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.500
The only thing missing
was probably the noise.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.630
There's a little bit more noise to it,

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.740
but there's not big balls of fire,

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.590
there's no walls falling
in and falling down,

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.265
that's exactly as it is.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.530
It's an Arnie movie,

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.470
the way he's dressed is just ridiculous,

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.810
it's all about, "Look at my image,"

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.070
as opposed to what I'm trying to do.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.287
He's got weapons and guns all over him.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.613
He just fired a nuclear
weapon from his shoulder.

00:03:10.613 --> 00:03:12.663
I mean, that is just ridiculous, you know.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.680
I've never even seen that sort
of rocket launcher anyway.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:17.720
And the other thing is

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.170
the enemy are running along

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.400
and firing from down here,

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.880
from the hip for some strange reason

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.040
and running in front of each other,

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.210
but no one seems to be shooting.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.800
It's just f------ ridiculous, you know,

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.450
he stood behind a couple of leaves

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:30.600
and no one can hit him.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:33.740
Wow.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.460
One of those nuclear grenades again

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.960
that seem to just destroy everything

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.259
in a 50-mile radius.

00:03:40.259 --> 00:03:41.917
Totally unrealistic.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.780
Soldier: Of course you're
afraid. You get your...

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.080
Billy: OK, my biggest criticism there is

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.210
you're on operations,

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.110
you're already in the enemy
territory behind the lines,

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.260
and your weapons should already be done

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.093
and ready to go.

00:03:59.093 --> 00:04:00.960
If they're not caught out in the open

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.640
then it's a bad use of ground.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.398
They should have been in cover.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.620
What the anti-tank weapons could do

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.640
that they've just fired, which is the 66,

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.620
again totally unrealistic,

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.060
unless it's a fuel bowser, it
wouldn't burst into flames,

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.019
so that's just for effect.

00:04:30.951 --> 00:04:32.640
Chris Kyle: He has eyes on our guys.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.040
Dandridge: Can you confirm it's him?

00:04:37.012 --> 00:04:37.929
Chris: It's him.

00:04:39.421 --> 00:04:41.790
Oh, it's him.
Billy: Right.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.120
You know, people do long-distance shots,

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.430
and to say that's over a mile

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.760
and being able to confirm
firstly that's the target

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.030
is, I would say, virtually impossible.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:52.960
Because of the distance,

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.610
no matter how good the sights are,

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.800
and also it's a desert terrain,

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.380
you'd normally get the heat rising

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:02.200
so there'd be some sort
of distraction between.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.970
If it's not the heat naturally
coming off the ground,

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.800
then out there it's
heat from the buildings.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.520
It may be a miracle day

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.960
where it was totally calm
and there's no heat rise,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.380
which I find...I've never known it,

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.810
having been a sniper.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.102
You can see it's a target,
I'll give him that,

00:05:17.102 --> 00:05:19.097
and, you know, it's worth a shot.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.400
You may have seen him fall;

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.952
it doesn't mean he's been hit.

00:05:26.952 --> 00:05:28.240
It doesn't mean he's dead.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.930
So they're the questionable
things, I would say,

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.840
but however, an amazing job,

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.930
and amazing things that snipers can do.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.256
It is possible.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.937
David Budd: Stay down! The
bullets can pierce the windows,

00:05:41.937 --> 00:05:44.561
but they can't get
through the armored metal.

00:05:44.561 --> 00:05:45.967
Control, Sierra Zulu Seven Nine,

00:05:45.967 --> 00:05:48.000
status: zero Thornton Circus.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.540
Control, Sierra Zulu Seven Nine,

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.290
status: zero Thornton Circus.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.123
Lavender....

00:05:52.123 --> 00:05:54.670
Billy: His sole job is to
protect that principal,

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:57.680
so, reality, rather than
curling up in his own seat,

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.170
I would have crawled into the back

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.160
and got hold of her

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.060
because you don't know
what she's gonna do.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:02.893
Is she gonna panic?

00:06:02.893 --> 00:06:04.560
Is she gonna raise her
head into the glass?

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:05.780
He really should have reacted better

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.490
by being on top of her,

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:09.230
getting her down low in the rear wheel

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:10.813
and protecting her.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.316
David: Shooter's located on roof of

00:06:13.316 --> 00:06:14.810
Pascoe House, one, zero, zero.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:15.750
Billy: If he got her out of the vehicle,

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.490
get down with her and get her moving,

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:18.800
he's now starting to,

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:22.550
you know, try and take
control of the vehicle,

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:24.663
which he should have done
from the start, to be honest.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.130
And again, realistically,

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.560
he's already said there's one sniper,

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:31.480
which how he identified
was a bit unrealistic.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.870
He should have just took
her up a side street,

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.250
you can't see everywhere

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.853
from any sniper position, so.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.810
Right now, the biggest problem with this,

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:42.910
if you're a bodyguard,

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:47.140
well, his primary role is
to look after a principal.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.118
He's now left her unattended,

00:06:49.118 --> 00:06:50.751
all on her own, to go and be a hero.

00:06:50.751 --> 00:06:52.690
Then he took himself out of the vehicle,

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.030
leaving her vulnerable,

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.420
then he's now left the
vehicle to become a hero.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.210
Where is she? She's on her own.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:00.243
Totally not doing a bodyguard's job.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.888
Jack Ryan: Camp 18.
Operator: Enlarging.

00:07:05.827 --> 00:07:08.505
Jack: Enlarge primary target.
Operator: Enlarging.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:14.530
Billy: OK, that's a view
initially from the operations room

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.160
as an operation is taking place,

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.900
which again is pretty realistic

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:21.370
in terms of the atmosphere
inside the operation room,

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.450
when it's going down.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:23.760
Everybody's watching all the radars,

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.500
watching the TVs, listening
to the communications,

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.880
and everybody's got their
heart in their mouth

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.516
and not really saying a lot.

00:07:30.386 --> 00:07:32.378
Operator: Airborne support approaching.

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.170
Billy: Put a little bit more detail,

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.140
and I've never actually seen it myself,

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.307
but it's pretty realistic.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.091
The wearing of shades,

00:07:50.091 --> 00:07:51.366
it's very much an Hollywood thing.

00:07:51.366 --> 00:07:52.810
That doesn't happen.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.260
So, as you're moving through shade,

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:56.370
you lose all perspective.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.650
All right, so that's the only fault

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.290
that we see with the
equipment and movement

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.550
from the start.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.080
Soldier: You mean fall off?
Soldier: Yeah.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.750
Billy: What they were
actually doing, again,

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.130
is not unrealistic as in terms of tasks

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.800
that the military would do.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.420
It would be done a lot more covertly.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.650
It was a little bit loud,

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.670
they were not cammed up.

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.060
For whatever reason,

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:16.537
which I find a little bit unrealistic

00:08:16.537 --> 00:08:18.520
is the bunching up, where
they all just come together

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.100
knowing full well that
they're being shot at.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.230
The big drill is to stay
away from each other,

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.855
'cause the more together,
the bigger the target.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:34.570
Where the rocket-propeller
grenade, the RPG-7, landed

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.940
and all of a sudden everybody's
catapulted in the air,

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:38.630
totally unrealistic.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:39.463
What it actually does,

00:08:39.463 --> 00:08:41.010
it would blow you off
your feet to a degree,

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.620
but you'd be covered in shrapnel

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.000
and probably have body parts missing.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.660
So it's a little bit Hollywoodized

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.320
with the rolling down the hill

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.128
and all the rest of the stuff.

00:08:51.128 --> 00:08:52.180
Marcus Luttrell: Oh, my rifle.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:54.820
Billy: The weapon is not
a massive priority really.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.440
If it was a person left behind, yes.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:57.420
They've been in contact,

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.383
they've managed to break
contact by falling back,

00:09:00.383 --> 00:09:02.040
and now they're hidden again.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.410
They've really given
their position away again

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.880
by talking too loud

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.396
and not moving and getting
the hell out of it.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:13.293
Stop!

00:09:13.293 --> 00:09:14.490
They're flying through the air,

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:17.060
hanging off the bottom
of an helicopter, no.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:18.636
That does not happen.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.330
OK, some of the explosive entry drills,

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.360
the window charges, pretty realistic,

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:31.000
the door, shotgun drills on the door,

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.440
again, realistic.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:35.260
Also there's grenades being
thrown around in there.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.880
Most of this is stun grenades

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.750
as opposed to fragmentation grenades.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:42.470
The equipment they're
wearing, from what I can see,

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.030
again is pretty realistic.

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:46.240
The synchronized abseiling down the wall

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:47.760
is a little bit dramatic.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:49.840
'Cause it takes a while
to set up an abseil

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:50.840
and do all that sort of stuff.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:53.000
You just wouldn't have
time to be able to do that.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.090
It's not like you see in "Spider-Man,"

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.358
where you can just attach it and go.

00:09:56.358 --> 00:09:57.660
Gotta get into position,

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.770
and then once it goes [snaps]
noise, and then you go,

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:02.478
but it's not synchronized abseiling.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.350
Did people get hung up
on churches and trees?

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:12.570
Yes, they did.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.390
You know, when they jumped
into and around villages,

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:16.740
you got blown all over the place

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:17.750
or you were dropped in the wrong place,

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.060
so that can happen.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.030
The way that probably happened

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:24.067
is a little bit, sort
of, again unrealistic.

00:10:24.067 --> 00:10:25.845
You know, you come down
with one hell of a smash

00:10:25.845 --> 00:10:28.120
and you'd probably get badly injured

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.220
as opposed to bounce around

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:30.728
like you're on a bouncy castle.

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:40.240
He's still got his reserve
parachute attached to him,

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.410
and the way to get down
is pull that parachute,

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.830
'cause then it'll drop down to the ground.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:46.940
Unattach one side and then climb down it.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:48.170
For whatever reason, he decides

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:51.180
to watch the show going
on below him for a while,

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.340
and then decides, "Oh,
maybe I should get out,"

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.240
and then starts cutting himself away, so.

00:10:59.834 --> 00:11:01.470
There's bullets and bombs
going off all around him,

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.260
but the German is alerted to the knife fall,

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.010
which is a bit weird.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:13.040
Private Ryan: Over the side!

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.163
Billy: The chaos of it all,

00:11:16.862 --> 00:11:20.670
the ridiculous sort of
obstacles you come up against,

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:22.010
which is not just bullets and bombs,

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:23.530
the water getting off a boat.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:27.220
So I think this is portrayed
really, really well.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:30.340
And having seen the
tracer lines of the rounds

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:31.830
going through the water,

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.810
although I've not been shot at underwater,

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:35.340
I have seen the effects
of firing through water,

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:37.460
and that, in my eyes, in my opinion,

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.123
is pretty realistic.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:47.830
Billy: I've seen people
shot in the f------ water.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:50.874
I mean, it goes off at
a tangent, but if you,

00:11:50.874 --> 00:11:52.810
you're firing at a bunch of people,

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.200
you're firing randomly,

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.940
it's quite likely that something,

